{"title":"2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A company builds cylinders. Its Model A cylinder has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593cebfe2f4feac91cf23dfc53f17cb2efc5f235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> cm and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a2062939a88eb6056ea6d7a9ebd30a5ff002efa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> cm.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Volume of a Cylinder: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/44184a0036f93527b56504656042f5e7ca069040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = \\pi r^{2}h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The company also builds a Model B cylinder having a radius of 8 cm. Each Model B cylinder has the same volume as each Model A cylinder. What is the height in cm of a Model B cylinder?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/38426b36116245ea1f41d7f25e82f441727cace6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the height in cm of a Model B cylinder.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a</a>, the volume of a Model A cylinder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d36027220f5aebe49a6eed48a376960613bf11a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600\\pi \\text{ cm}^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The volume of the Model B cylinder would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f7b4030d9cda1184d622a59072134e93696061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\times 8^{2} \\times h = 64\\pi h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff7fa61ea98f938205e19efb28f60df2029013a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ cm}^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" />. Since this is equal to the volume of a Model A cylinder, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf7afc317d44e0ddd3b106d41f4e1fa919d2567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64\\pi h = 1600\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/6568dd6a4cb71101907ff8e1c51e5d52af5a800a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\frac{1600\\pi}{64\\pi} = \\boxed{25 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that multiplying the radius of the Model A cylinder by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0b7390aae7ac332ed45fddb9d6a7a69e8eff6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{10} = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" /> gives the radius of the Model B cylinder. This means that, if the height of the cylinders were the same, the volume of the Model B cylinder would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea695cfb442480b7e6b2117e9dc2cab6a23eada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{4}{5})^{2} = \\frac{4^{2}}{5^{2}} = \\frac{16}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" /> times the volume of the Model A cylinder.\n</p><p>Thus, the height of the Model B cylinder must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658d34fe4c66abc876b78ad047b34566b2d8360a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> times the height of the Model A cylinder, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6afbdb20dc9f1a910a2c2e749b7b8dc445a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{16} \\times 16 = \\boxed{25 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000343\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.114 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 71/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 965/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2528/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.861      1 2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   14.861      1 -total\n 39.73%    5.904      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36962:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000343 and revision id 285851. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}